   "source": [
    "# Example of Assignment 2\n",
    "\n",
    "The idea behind assignment 2 is to use develop two ML models which recognizes emotions from images (sad face, happy, surprised, etc.). In order to achieve this, there are a few technical challenges that should be tackle, such as data imbalance, choosing the right features for the datastet, normalization strategies, etc. \n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a basic example of a pipeline that a random forest with landmarks and evaluates the model to compute the confusion matrix, (balanced)accuracy and F1 macro."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Loading and perform feature extraction on the dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "b5ef313f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, confusion_matrix\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we compute the class weights for the training set"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "429929f4-efca-4ab1-b218-4a9a998772a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "csv_file = './data/fer2013_train.csv'\n",
    "model_file = \"./models/rf_fer_model_landmarks.pkl\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Loading the data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "b9807f11",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "###############################\n",
    "# Computing class weights\n",
    "##############################\n",
    "from sklearn.utils.class_weight import compute_class_weight\n",
    "\n",
    "trai_df = pd.read_csv(csv_file)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Computing class weights for unbalanced dataset\n",
    "labelsTrain = trai_df['emotion'].values\n",
    "cw = compute_class_weight(\n",
    "    class_weight=\"balanced\", classes=np.unique(labelsTrain), y=labelsTrain)\n",
    "#class_weights = {0:cw[0],1:cw[1],2:cw[2], 3:cw[3], 4:cw[4], 5:cw[5], 6:cw[6]}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### This is an example of a feature extraction pipeline\n",
    "For this simple baseline model, we use a simple feature extraction pipeline with landmarks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "182f07bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import dlib \n",
    "\n",
    "# Importing dlib's landmark detector\n",
    "# Dlib landmarks from: \n",
    "#   https://github.com/davisking/dlib-models/blob/master/shape_predictor_68_face_landmarks.dat.bz2\n",
    "landmDet = dlib.shape_predictor(\"faceAndLandmarkModels/shape_predictor_68_face_landmarks_GTX.dat\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize scaler and classifier\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Track if scaler is fitted\n",
    "scaler_fitted = False\n",
    "\n",
    "def extractLandmarksFER(images):\n",
    "    face_rects = dlib.rectangle(left=1, top=1, right=47, bottom=47)\n",
    "    x1 = face_rects.left() \n",
    "    y1 = face_rects.top() \n",
    "    x2 = face_rects.right() \n",
    "    y2 = face_rects.bottom()\n",
    "\n",
    "    landm = []\n",
    "    for img in images:\n",
    "        la = landmDet(img.astype(np.uint8), face_rects)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # This works better if the standard scaler is not usec\n",
    "        la2 = np.asarray( np.matrix([\n",
    "            [\n",
    "                (p.x-0.5*(x2-x1))/(x2-x1), (p.y-0.5*(y2-y1))/(y2-y1)\n",
    "            ] for p in la.parts()])).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "        la2 -= np.mean(la2, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n",
    "        la2 /= np.max(np.abs(la2), axis=0, keepdims=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "        landm.append(la2.flatten())\n",
    "    feats = np.stack(landm)\n",
    "    return(feats)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Loading the images\n",
    "images = np.array(\n",
    "        [np.fromstring(pixels, sep=' ').reshape(48, 48) for pixels in trai_df['pixels']])\n",
    "feats = extractLandmarksFER(images)\n",
    "\n",
    "images = None"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Evaluating the results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "823659d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Model saved to ./models/rf_fer_model_landmarks.pkl\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "rf = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=300,       # Number of trees\n",
    "    max_depth=11,           # Allow trees to grow fully\n",
    "    max_features='sqrt',   # Use sqrt(features) for splitting\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1,             # Use all available CPU cores \n",
    "    #class_weight= \"balanced\", #class_weights,\n",
    "    criterion=\"entropy\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "rf.fit(feats, trai_df['emotion'].values)\n",
    "\n",
    "joblib.dump(rf, model_file)\n",
    "print(f\"Model saved to {model_file}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Finally, now that we have the trained models, we perfom the performance measurements in the validation set"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "258fedfa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Accuracy: 0.45\n",
      "Balanced accuracy: 0.38\n",
      "Macro F1: 0.38\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def preprocessingFer(dataFrame):\n",
    "    # Convert pixel strings to 48x48 images\n",
    "    images = np.array(\n",
    "        [np.fromstring(pixels, sep=' ').reshape(48, 48) for pixels in dataFrame['pixels']])\n",
    "    X =  extractLandmarksFER(images)\n",
    "    y = dataFrame['emotion'].values\n",
    "    return([X,y])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predict and evaluate\n",
    "valid = pd.read_csv('./data/fer2013_validation.csv')\n",
    "X_valid, y_valid = preprocessingFer(valid)\n",
    "\n",
    "y_pred = rf.predict(X_valid)\n",
    "accuracy = accuracy_score(y_valid, y_pred)\n",
    "conf_matrix = confusion_matrix(y_valid, y_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import balanced_accuracy_score, f1_score\n",
    "baccuracy = balanced_accuracy_score(y_valid, y_pred)\n",
    "macro_f1 = f1_score(y_valid, y_pred, average='macro')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print results\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy: {accuracy:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Balanced accuracy: {baccuracy:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Macro F1: {macro_f1:.2f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(conf_matrix, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Confusion Matrix only landmarks\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Predicted\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Actual\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Our FER2013 Experiments\n",
    "\n",
    "The sections below extend the provided Random Forest and landmark example. We compare LR, SVM, and RF with landmarks, HOG, and PCA features. We use validation results to choose the model settings, then evaluate the selected model on PrivateTest.\n",
    "\n",
    "Accuracy is the share of correct predictions. Balanced accuracy averages recall across classes. Macro F1 gives each class the same weight. These scores help us compare models when class sizes differ.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
