  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. PCA Features from Raw Pixels\n",
    "\n",
    "We scale pixel values to the range 0–1 and apply PCA to the 2,304 raw pixel values per image. We keep 150 components as an initial setting. PCA is fitted only on the training set and then used to transform the validation set.\n",
    "\n",
    "The 150 components keep 92.31% of the training pixel variance. This is not classification accuracy. PCA keeps large changes in the pixels, which may not be the changes that best separate expressions. We apply PCA to raw pixels, rather than to HOG or landmarks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "06f12140",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training PCA: (28709, 150)\n",
      "Validation PCA: (3589, 150)\n",
      "Explained variance: 92.31%\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "['./models/pca_fer_pixels.pkl']"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 13,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract_pixel_features(data_frame):\n",
    "    return np.stack([\n",
    "        np.fromstring(pixels, sep=\" \", dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "        for pixels in data_frame[\"pixels\"]\n",
    "    ]) / 255.0\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_pixels = extract_pixel_features(trai_df)\n",
    "X_valid_pixels = extract_pixel_features(valid)\n",
    "\n",
    "pca = PCA(\n",
    "    n_components=150,\n",
    "    svd_solver=\"randomized\",\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fit PCA only on the training set\n",
    "X_train_pca = pca.fit_transform(X_train_pixels)\n",
    "X_valid_pca = pca.transform(X_valid_pixels)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training PCA:\", X_train_pca.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Validation PCA:\", X_valid_pca.shape)\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    \"Explained variance:\",\n",
    "    f\"{pca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum():.2%}\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "joblib.dump(pca, \"./models/pca_fer_pixels.pkl\")"
   ]
  },
